meta {
  name: Get Own Privacy Settings
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.community.actor.getPrivacySettings?actor={{did}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

params:query {
  actor: {{did}}
}

docs {
  # Get Own Privacy Settings
  
  Retrieves the privacy settings for the authenticated user's own profile.
  
  ## Query Parameters
  - `actor` (string): The DID or handle of the user (use own DID for own settings)
  
  ## Response
  Returns privacy settings information:
  - `isPrivate`: Whether the profile is private
  - `isOwnProfile`: true (when viewing own settings)
  - `canView`: true (owner can always view own profile)
  - `allowedFollowers`: Array of DIDs that are approved followers (if private)
  
  ## Test Scenario
  Used to verify privacy settings after making changes:
  1. User authenticates
  2. User sets privacy to private
  3. User retrieves own privacy settings
  4. Verify isPrivate is true
  5. Verify allowedFollowers list is accessible
  
  **Note:** When viewing own settings, you always have full access to all privacy information.
}
